1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,260
Maven is one build tool. Gradle is the other big one, and many teams use it every day.

2
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:12,634
In this lesson you read a real Gradle project, file by file, and you learn four ideas.

3
00:00:13,184 --> 00:00:16,747
The project. The build script. The wrapper. And the task graph.

4
00:00:17,297 --> 00:00:19,143
You will watch all of it live,

5
00:00:19,143 --> 00:00:20,189
on a real Gradle,

6
00:00:20,189 --> 00:00:23,142
from the simplest command to a task of your own.

7
00:00:23,692 --> 00:00:26,807
Then you do it alone, and a checker judges your result.

8
00:00:27,357 --> 00:00:30,706
One idea first: everything Gradle does is a task.

9
00:00:32,256 --> 00:00:34,816
Four ideas explain every Gradle build.

10
00:00:35,366 --> 00:00:39,483
One, the project. A folder, with a settings file that gives it a name.

11
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:40,276
Two,

12
00:00:40,276 --> 00:00:41,306
the build script,

13
00:00:41,306 --> 00:00:42,337
build dot gradle.

14
00:00:42,337 --> 00:00:43,610
It lists the plugins,

15
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:44,337
the version,

16
00:00:44,337 --> 00:00:46,156
and where libraries come from.

17
00:00:46,706 --> 00:00:47,159
Three,

18
00:00:47,159 --> 00:00:48,065
the wrapper.

19
00:00:48,065 --> 00:00:49,197
A small script,

20
00:00:49,197 --> 00:00:49,876
gradle W,

21
00:00:49,876 --> 00:00:55,161
that downloads and runs the exact Gradle version the project asks for.

22
00:00:55,161 --> 00:00:57,501
Nobody installs Gradle by hand.

23
00:00:58,051 --> 00:00:58,407
Four,

24
00:00:58,407 --> 00:00:58,835
tasks.

25
00:00:58,835 --> 00:01:01,188
Everything Gradle does is a task,

26
00:01:01,188 --> 00:01:03,471
and tasks depend on other tasks.

27
00:01:03,471 --> 00:01:05,539
That chain is the task graph.

28
00:01:06,089 --> 00:01:11,379
Maven gives you a fixed lifecycle. Gradle lets you shape the graph. Let us see it live.

29
00:01:13,429 --> 00:01:19,402
Go into the project. Type: CD, slash opt, slash lab ninety-five, slash cartcore.

30
00:01:19,952 --> 00:01:22,022
List the folder. Type: L S.

31
00:01:22,572 --> 00:01:23,913
Five things matter.

32
00:01:23,913 --> 00:01:25,113
Build dot gradle,

33
00:01:25,113 --> 00:01:26,313
the build script.

34
00:01:26,313 --> 00:01:27,725
Settings dot gradle,

35
00:01:27,725 --> 00:01:29,208
the project settings.

36
00:01:29,208 --> 00:01:29,844
Gradle W,

37
00:01:29,844 --> 00:01:31,185
the wrapper script,

38
00:01:31,185 --> 00:01:33,303
with its folder called gradle.

39
00:01:33,303 --> 00:01:34,715
And the source code,

40
00:01:34,715 --> 00:01:35,350
in S R C.

41
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:39,826
Open the project settings. Type: cat, settings dot gradle.

42
00:01:40,376 --> 00:01:40,980
One line.

43
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,399
The root project is named cart core.

44
00:01:43,399 --> 00:01:45,347
This name is used in the jar,

45
00:01:45,347 --> 00:01:46,690
and in every report.

46
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,678
Now the build script,

47
00:01:48,678 --> 00:01:50,321
without its empty lines.

48
00:01:50,321 --> 00:01:51,075
Type: grep,

49
00:01:51,075 --> 00:01:51,554
dash v,

50
00:01:51,554 --> 00:01:51,965
quote,

51
00:01:51,965 --> 00:01:52,376
caret,

52
00:01:52,376 --> 00:01:52,855
dollar,

53
00:01:52,855 --> 00:01:53,266
quote,

54
00:01:53,266 --> 00:01:54,430
build dot gradle.

55
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:55,953
Plugins: java.

56
00:01:55,953 --> 00:01:58,108
That one word adds the compile,

57
00:01:58,108 --> 00:01:59,428
test and jar tasks.

58
00:01:59,428 --> 00:02:01,931
Group and version name the artifact.

59
00:02:01,931 --> 00:02:04,989
Repositories says where libraries come from.

60
00:02:04,989 --> 00:02:07,630
And the jar block sets the main class.

61
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:09,269
Now the wrapper.

62
00:02:09,269 --> 00:02:13,080
Keep only the download address from its properties file.

63
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:13,829
Type: grep,

64
00:02:13,829 --> 00:02:15,122
distribution U R L,

65
00:02:15,122 --> 00:02:16,619
then the path: gradle,

66
00:02:16,619 --> 00:02:17,572
slash wrapper,

67
00:02:17,572 --> 00:02:20,362
slash gradle dash wrapper dot properties.

68
00:02:20,912 --> 00:02:22,088
The exact address,

69
00:02:22,088 --> 00:02:24,114
on services dot gradle dot org,

70
00:02:24,114 --> 00:02:28,231
and the exact version: Gradle eight point fourteen point three.

71
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:29,276
Every developer,

72
00:02:29,276 --> 00:02:30,779
and every build server,

73
00:02:30,779 --> 00:02:32,282
gets this same version.

74
00:02:32,832 --> 00:02:33,844
One honest note.

75
00:02:33,844 --> 00:02:36,878
In my recording studio that download is blocked,

76
00:02:36,878 --> 00:02:39,976
so a copy of the same version was already stored.

77
00:02:39,976 --> 00:02:40,987
On your machine,

78
00:02:40,987 --> 00:02:42,694
the first run downloads it,

79
00:02:42,694 --> 00:02:44,907
about one hundred thirty megabytes.

80
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:46,608
Run the wrapper,

81
00:02:46,608 --> 00:02:48,335
and ask for its version.

82
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:50,134
Type: dot slash gradle W,

83
00:02:50,134 --> 00:02:51,429
dash dash version,

84
00:02:51,429 --> 00:02:52,796
and keep two lines.

85
00:02:54,846 --> 00:02:57,452
Gradle eight point fourteen point three,

86
00:02:57,452 --> 00:02:58,690
on Java twenty-one.

87
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:00,579
The project chose its Gradle.

88
00:03:00,579 --> 00:03:02,078
You did not install it.

89
00:03:02,628 --> 00:03:04,110
Everything is a task.

90
00:03:04,110 --> 00:03:06,509
List the tasks of the build group.

91
00:03:06,509 --> 00:03:08,274
Type: dot slash gradle W,

92
00:03:08,274 --> 00:03:08,697
tasks,

93
00:03:08,697 --> 00:03:10,744
dash dash group equals build,

94
00:03:10,744 --> 00:03:12,932
and keep the lines with a dash.

95
00:03:15,282 --> 00:03:15,896
Assemble,

96
00:03:15,896 --> 00:03:16,306
build,

97
00:03:16,306 --> 00:03:16,853
classes,

98
00:03:16,853 --> 00:03:17,263
clean,

99
00:03:17,263 --> 00:03:17,536
jar.

100
00:03:17,536 --> 00:03:18,902
Each line is a task,

101
00:03:18,902 --> 00:03:20,336
with its description.

102
00:03:20,336 --> 00:03:22,727
Build is the one you will use most.

103
00:03:23,277 --> 00:03:24,639
Now the task graph.

104
00:03:24,639 --> 00:03:26,860
Ask Gradle what build would do,

105
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,079
without doing it.

106
00:03:28,079 --> 00:03:29,870
Type: dot slash gradle W,

107
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:30,300
build,

108
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:30,802
dash m,

109
00:03:30,802 --> 00:03:32,450
and head dash n twelve.

110
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,440
Compile java,

111
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,379
then classes,

112
00:03:36,379 --> 00:03:37,029
then jar,

113
00:03:37,029 --> 00:03:38,041
then assemble,

114
00:03:38,041 --> 00:03:38,474
check,

115
00:03:38,474 --> 00:03:39,775
and finally build.

116
00:03:39,775 --> 00:03:41,870
The dash m flag is a dry run.

117
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:43,315
It prints the order,

118
00:03:43,315 --> 00:03:44,544
and runs nothing.

119
00:03:44,544 --> 00:03:46,639
This order is the task graph.

120
00:03:47,189 --> 00:03:48,620
Now run it for real.

121
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,410
Keep the build line and the task count.

122
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:53,199
Type: dot slash gradle W,

123
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:53,628
build,

124
00:03:53,628 --> 00:03:54,272
and grep.

125
00:03:56,322 --> 00:03:57,487
Build successful.

126
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:58,927
Two actionable tasks,

127
00:03:58,927 --> 00:03:59,818
two executed.

128
00:03:59,818 --> 00:04:01,258
It compiled the code,

129
00:04:01,258 --> 00:04:02,423
and made the jar.

130
00:04:02,973 --> 00:04:04,488
Run the same command again.

131
00:04:08,138 --> 00:04:09,559
Two actionable tasks,

132
00:04:09,559 --> 00:04:10,575
two up to date.

133
00:04:10,575 --> 00:04:11,658
Nothing changed,

134
00:04:11,658 --> 00:04:13,147
so Gradle did no work.

135
00:04:13,147 --> 00:04:18,292
That is why Gradle is fast: it skips every task whose inputs did not change.

136
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:22,725
Change the build script, with sed. The version becomes one point one.

137
00:04:24,775 --> 00:04:25,861
Build quietly,

138
00:04:25,861 --> 00:04:27,257
and list the jars.

139
00:04:27,257 --> 00:04:29,196
Type: dot slash gradle W,

140
00:04:29,196 --> 00:04:29,661
build,

141
00:04:29,661 --> 00:04:30,204
dash q,

142
00:04:30,204 --> 00:04:30,902
then L S,

143
00:04:30,902 --> 00:04:31,367
build,

144
00:04:31,367 --> 00:04:32,220
slash libs.

145
00:04:34,570 --> 00:04:35,967
A new jar: cart core,

146
00:04:35,967 --> 00:04:36,899
one point one.

147
00:04:36,899 --> 00:04:41,024
The version in the script became the version in the file name.

148
00:04:41,024 --> 00:04:42,221
The old jar stays,

149
00:04:42,221 --> 00:04:43,552
until you run clean.

150
00:04:44,102 --> 00:04:44,412
Last,

151
00:04:44,412 --> 00:04:45,590
a task of your own.

152
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:48,628
Add one line to the script: a task called report,

153
00:04:48,628 --> 00:04:49,992
that depends on build,

154
00:04:49,992 --> 00:04:52,720
and prints the project name and the version.

155
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:59,053
Run it. Type: dot slash gradle W, dash q, report.

156
00:05:01,103 --> 00:05:01,709
Cart core,

157
00:05:01,709 --> 00:05:02,557
one point one.

158
00:05:02,557 --> 00:05:03,406
Your task ran,

159
00:05:03,406 --> 00:05:06,618
and it read the name and the version from the script,

160
00:05:06,618 --> 00:05:07,951
not from your fingers.

161
00:05:08,501 --> 00:05:11,872
Does build run first? Ask for the graph, and keep two lines.

162
00:05:13,922 --> 00:05:14,320
Build,

163
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,384
and then report.

164
00:05:15,384 --> 00:05:16,846
Because of depends on,

165
00:05:16,846 --> 00:05:18,441
Gradle runs build first.

166
00:05:18,441 --> 00:05:20,834
One line of yours changed the graph.

167
00:05:22,384 --> 00:05:25,904
Your task. The same journey, on your own project, in the lab.

168
00:05:26,454 --> 00:05:28,157
One: in build dot gradle,

169
00:05:28,157 --> 00:05:30,405
set the version to one point one,

170
00:05:30,405 --> 00:05:31,086
and build.

171
00:05:31,086 --> 00:05:34,561
The jar must be named cart core dash one point one.

172
00:05:35,111 --> 00:05:39,527
Two: add a task named report, that prints the project name and the version.

173
00:05:40,077 --> 00:05:42,210
Three: make report depend on build.

174
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:47,880
Four: save the task graph, from dash dash dry dash run, in graph dot text.

175
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:52,782
Five: write notes dot text, three lines: settings, wrapper, and task.

176
00:05:54,832 --> 00:05:59,035
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

177
00:05:59,585 --> 00:06:01,284
The lab lives on git hub,

178
00:06:01,284 --> 00:06:02,439
at it dash waves,

179
00:06:02,439 --> 00:06:04,002
slash dev ops dash A I,

180
00:06:04,002 --> 00:06:05,497
in the folder academy,

181
00:06:05,497 --> 00:06:06,177
slash lab.

182
00:06:06,727 --> 00:06:12,017
Two files: lab ninety-five dot S H, and shortcuts ninety-five dot S H.

183
00:06:12,567 --> 00:06:13,443
Install it,

184
00:06:13,443 --> 00:06:17,026
in your Ubuntu virtual machine: sudo install,

185
00:06:17,026 --> 00:06:18,858
dash m seven five five,

186
00:06:18,858 --> 00:06:20,769
lab ninety-five dot S H,

187
00:06:20,769 --> 00:06:21,963
into slash usr,

188
00:06:21,963 --> 00:06:22,919
slash local,

189
00:06:22,919 --> 00:06:23,874
slash S bin.

190
00:06:24,424 --> 00:06:28,636
Load the short name with: source shortcuts ninety-five dot S H.

191
00:06:28,636 --> 00:06:30,374
Then you can type: lab up,

192
00:06:30,374 --> 00:06:31,043
lab check,

193
00:06:31,043 --> 00:06:31,912
and lab down.

194
00:06:32,462 --> 00:06:33,603
You need a J D K,

195
00:06:33,603 --> 00:06:35,080
curl and python three,

196
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:37,026
about one gigabyte of memory,

197
00:06:37,026 --> 00:06:38,839
and an internet connection.

198
00:06:38,839 --> 00:06:41,121
The first lab up downloads Gradle,

199
00:06:41,121 --> 00:06:43,470
about one hundred thirty megabytes.

200
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:48,308
Lab down removes everything. Only run it in your own virtual machine.

201
00:06:50,358 --> 00:06:52,427
Pass or fail. You need all six.

202
00:06:52,977 --> 00:06:54,791
Five pass lines in lab check.

203
00:06:55,341 --> 00:06:58,263
The version comes from the script, not typed by hand.

204
00:06:58,813 --> 00:07:01,139
You used the wrapper, not another Gradle.

205
00:07:01,689 --> 00:07:03,758
Graph dot text shows the right order.

206
00:07:04,308 --> 00:07:06,441
Notes dot text is in your own words.

207
00:07:06,991 --> 00:07:08,847
Lab down leaves nothing behind.

208
00:07:09,397 --> 00:07:10,699
To pass, all six.

209
00:07:12,749 --> 00:07:15,586
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

210
00:07:16,136 --> 00:07:18,227
One: lab up, and read the task file.

211
00:07:18,777 --> 00:07:21,593
Two: open the project, and look at every file.

212
00:07:22,143 --> 00:07:24,852
Three: change the version, and build with the wrapper.

213
00:07:25,402 --> 00:07:28,581
Four: add the report task, and make it depend on build.

214
00:07:29,131 --> 00:07:32,310
Five: save the graph, write the notes, and run lab check.

215
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:35,441
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

216
00:07:35,991 --> 00:07:37,826
Pause the video, and begin now.

217
00:07:53,376 --> 00:07:54,251
Quick check.

218
00:07:54,801 --> 00:07:56,827
Which file gives the project its name?

219
00:07:57,377 --> 00:07:59,425
What does the wrapper do, and why use it?

220
00:07:59,975 --> 00:08:01,234
What is a task graph?

221
00:08:01,784 --> 00:08:03,235
What does up to date mean?

222
00:08:03,785 --> 00:08:10,078
Objective covered: M C eleven, objective one, Gradle projects, wrapper, scripts and tasks.

